      "Manifest exact bytes rehashed and reparsed, source identity/reopened path checked; command dict mutation cannot poison command(); closed installation remains closed. Constructor and factory initialize/start exception paths close installation; normal stop closes dispatcher/worker/ownership/installation.",
      "Linux caching requires actual held/current ST_RDONLY plus trusted immutable provisioning excluding writable aliases/mappings. Prior Linux evidence is pre-format; AST equivalence verified, no fresh Linux execution claimed. Writable/unknown platform uses streaming hashes.",
      "Factory initialization policy reads public spec inside trusted process; hostile mutation of verifier object/process is outside declared boundary. Later path execution is not atomic with verification."
